===== README.md =====
# Observer gateway route for Claude Desktop

**Not live-verified (LC2).** Nobody has yet confirmed that Claude Desktop accepts
`http://127.0.0.1:8820` as `inferenceGatewayBaseUrl` and that the proxy forwards the gateway
credential upstream. Deploy it to one machine and check that a Code-tab session
lands `api_turns` rows before a fleet rollout.

The Desktop Code tab ignores `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` from every settings file,
managed ones included: its only route is gateway mode. This policy sets
`inferenceProvider = gateway`, `inferenceGatewayBaseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8820`,
`inferenceGatewayAuthScheme = x-api-key` and `inferenceCredentialKind = helper-script`.

## What it costs

Claude Desktop routes only in gateway mode, which needs a gateway credential (an API key a credential helper prints, not a claude.ai sign-in) and drops Anthropic-hosted cloud environments and Remote Control; skip the route to keep them.
Use it for an API-key or org-gateway organization; a fleet that signs in to
claude.ai keeps the direct route.

## The credential

Observer never writes a key into the policy. The Desktop runs the helper you
deploy and sends what it prints as the gateway credential:

- Linux and macOS: `/usr/local/bin/org-gateway-key`
- Windows: `C:\Program Files\Org\gateway-key.exe`

Keep the helper administrator-owned: it runs on every launch. The proxy must be
running on the node; with it down, Desktop inference fails instead of going
direct.

## Deploy (one channel per machine)

- `cowork/managed-settings.json` (linux, /etc/claude-desktop/managed-settings.json):
  - sudo install -d -m 0755 -o root -g root "/etc/claude-desktop"
  - sudo install -m 0644 -o root -g root "managed-settings.json" "/etc/claude-desktop/managed-settings.json"
  - Fleet: ship the same file with your configuration management (Ansible, Puppet, Chef, Salt) or a package.
- `cowork/managed-settings.mobileconfig` (darwin, macos_profile):
  - Upload the .mobileconfig to your MDM (Jamf, Kandji, Mosyle, Intune) as a custom configuration profile scoped to the devices, or
  - for one test Mac: open the file, then System Settings > Privacy and Security > Profiles > Install.
  - The profile is unsigned: sign it with your MDM's certificate if your MDM requires signed profiles.
  - Check with: sudo profiles show -type configuration | grep com.anthropic.claudefordesktop
- `cowork/managed-settings.reg` (windows, windows_registry):
  - From an elevated prompt: reg import managed-settings.reg
  - Fleet: deploy the same values under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Claude with Group Policy Preferences (Registry) or an Intune configuration profile.
  - HKLM policy keys are writable by administrators only.
